# Typed by hand from Poettgen et al., J. Solid State Chem. 119 (1995) 324 (reference_papers/
# Pottgen1995_ScCrC2_JSSC119_324.pdf): Table 1, P6_3/mmc subcell of alpha-ScCrC2, a = 324.16(3), c = 915.0(1) pm
# (Guinier powder data); Table 2, subcell atoms Sc 2a, Cr 2c, C 4f z = 0.6624(8), ideal occupancies (as in the
# paper's final cycles), B_eq 0.32/1.06/1.11 A^2 -> U = B/(8 pi^2). This is the cell the plan names (3.2416/9.150).
# The single-crystal beta-ScCrC2 values (a 323.7, c 914.9 pm, C z 0.6627) differ by < 0.15 %.

